<title>NEW ZEALAND: Telecom buys back on mkt at up to NZ$7.15.</title>
<headline>Telecom buys back on mkt at up to NZ$7.15.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telecom Corp of New Zealand said on Tuesday it had acquired 28,100 shares on the market during the day at a range of prices up to NZ$7.15 each, pursuant to its $1 billion share buyback programme.</p>
<p>The shares were bought in three lots at $7.11, $7.12 and $7.15 respectively.</p>
<p>The current phase of Telecom's buyback is expected to continue until the company gives notice that it is completed.</p>
<p>Its shares closed Tuesday up 7.0 cents at $7.19.</p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
